<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George I of Great Britain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1660–1727</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as George Louis of Hanover, George Louis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George I, born George Louis, was elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> from 1698 and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> in 1714 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> through his mother Sophia, founding the Hanoverian dynasty. As elector he acquired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen-verden">Duchies of Bremen and Verden</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1715, a gain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> recognised in 1719. He lived mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, and Hanover was governed by a privy council.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-i-of-great-britain.jpg" alt="George I of Great Britain" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Godfrey Kneller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_George_I_by_Sir_Godfrey_Kneller,_Bt_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
